  "body": "Thanks, that makes sense and yes it's probably a blocker for official homebrew/cask.\n\nWould you consider a project-owned tap instead? The app would still need to be manually approved on first launch, but that is already the case with the current macOS distribution anyway.\n\nThe main benefit would be that users could install, update, and uninstall ART through Homebrew, e.g. `brew install --cask artraweditor/art/art`, even if it is not part of the official homebrew/cask tap. Using third-party taps is a fairly common and well-supported Homebrew workflow, especially for open-source software.",
